From 100bc1686a3eeca96380b1d4116abad1a7429a8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:31:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: input: syna,rmi4: constrain the panel follower
 reference

The LTS binding already describes an optional panel. Give that reference
its phandle type and prohibit it for SPI transports, matching the actual
I2C-only follower implementation. Preserve the existing LTS compatible
enum and all other device descriptions; do not import unrelated matches.

Actual-source host tests reproduce 16 touch and eight panel cleanup
failures before the changes and none afterward. Four targeted power/PM
regressions and three DSI command regressions are rejected. Native ARM,
ARM64 and ARM64 RT objects compile with nonpermissive CFI; built-in,
modular and DRM-disabled profiles are checked. All nineteen maintained
family/control DTBs validate against the full schema, with 25 focused
binding cases. Low-level I/O, runtime callback schedules and selected
core operations are modeled; real hardware and complete kernel driver
core execution, panel timing and RMI disable-failure recovery remain open.

Codex prepared this local reconciliation and qualification, preserving
the original author, date and source notices. Human DCO and review are
pending; no sign-off certification, phone action or publication is claimed.

Backported from commit 79c77fb2cafc ("dt-bindings: input: syna,rmi4:
describe an in-cell I2C panel")
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/syna,rmi4.yaml | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/syna,rmi4.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/syna,rmi4.yaml
index 545867d4b1e1..64f62c6d9908 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/syna,rmi4.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/syna,rmi4.yaml
@@ -35,9 +35,10 @@ properties:
     maxItems: 1
 
   panel:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
     description:
-      The panel an in-cell touchscreen belongs to. The touchscreen is then
-      powered down before the panel and powered up after it.
+      Display panel that must be powered on before the in-cell touchscreen.
+      The I2C controller follows the panel's prepare and unprepare sequence.
 
   reset-gpios:
     maxItems: 1
@@ -219,6 +220,7 @@ allOf:
         spi-tx-delay-us: false
     else:
       properties:
+        panel: false
         syna,reset-delay-ms: false
         syna,startup-delay-ms: false
 
-- 
2.56.0

